p(51,'Which coherent target is universal?',[202],'The recipient F_X should be functorially isomorphic to omega squared.','A classification must first impose a generated target or local epimorphism, a naturality category, and a finite-order condition.','C-SA04-201: direct-sum counterexample refutes the unrestricted target claim. Dumas§3.1–3.2 documents the classical target; HoshiDefinition1.2 fixes rather than classifies the target. Exact repaired universal quantifiers were not located.',['BDumas2009','BHoshi2024'],'Worth a focused formulation task: decide the smallest precise universal property before attempting a classification.')
p(52,'Uniqueness in a fixed characteristic',[204],'Conditions a,b,c and nonzero G0 characterize it up to a nonzero F_p scalar; margin faux?/order at most3.','Restrict to a specified finite-order polynomial-law or jet-natural operator category and distinguish p=2,3 from p>3.','C-SA04-203; Hoshi§3 concerns locally exact differentials in characteristic2, §6Remark6.4.2 its level-one degeneration; Wakabayashi§1.7 assumes oddp. No opened source proves the manuscript’s unrestricted fixed-p classification.',['BHoshi2024','BHoshi2020','BWakabayashi2021'],'High interest, but one short run should only formulate and calculate the order-three module, not claim the unrestricted theorem.')
p(53,'Is homogeneous target necessary?',[212],'The homogeneous value space seems a condition for success.','Specify what counts as an invariant quotient with local solvability and rigidity, then test homogeneous and nonhomogeneous actions.','C-SA04-211 is not yet a quantified theorem; Hoshi’s Schwarz systems are a comparison framework, not an answer to this necessity question.',['BHoshi2024'],'Low priority until the word success is made into exact axioms.')
p(54,'Proportional logarithmic derivatives',[218],'The terminal question tests dlogf proportional to dlogg as a vanishing condition.','Only the squared-equality case forces f=cg or c/g; an arbitrary exponent does not.','C-SA04-219 is refuted by t² andt on a punctured disc. Dumas§3.1 gives the classical projective vanishing criterion; exact computation is saved.',['BDumas2009'],'Resolved mathematically; next work is a scan check of the intended question.')
